\pard\sa120\keepn\b\fs34\cf2 VB.Net Basic Controls\b0\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab An object is a type of user interface element you create on a Visual Basic form by using a toolbox control. In fact, in Visual Basic, the form itself is an object. Every Visual Basic control consists of three important elements:\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Properties which describe the object,\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Methods cause an object to do something and\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Events are what happens when an object does something\par
